Z||000003||terryk||10-07-2001||01:27 PM||||Sorry, you said trans electronics, not electronic trans (4t6xE).<P>Depending on the model, there is TCC and 3rd and 4th gear switches. I think I have the wiring somewhere.<P>Send me an email and I will forward it to you. Problem is, the wiring is scattered over seeral pages.<P>It's a THM440-4/4T60. Same beast.<P>Should be wired like this:<P>Three connectors on the trans:<BR>1. Above the modulator. Round (TCC and gear switches).<BR>2. On the shift selector (PN, trunk release, backup lights). <BR>3. On the opposite output shaft housing (VSS output).<P>Not using a stock ECM? I would guess the TCC control would be the first problem wire. I would assume this ECU would work with the VSS output. The PN switch so you can't start it in gear. The others are just trunk release and backup lights.<BR>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
